\ `times` holds its closure body in a spill for every iteration. When the body raises, the word's
\ error exit releases the spill, so the binary reports no leak.

count-down: ( n -- s ) [
  [ [ dup 1 - / drop ] curry 3 swap times "finished" ]
  [ 2drop "raised" ]
  recover
] ;

1 count-down print-line
2 count-down print-line
